### Title
Single confirmation when removing an environment

### Why
`conda env remove` and `conda remove --all` used to ask twice. The second question ran only after packages were already uninstalled, so declining it left a half-deleted environment. Removal should now ask once, before anything is deleted. (#16753 via #16852)

### Platforms
- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites
A conda build that includes this change. Network access to install one small package.

### Steps
1. `conda create -n qa-env-remove xz --yes`, then deactivate it.
2. `conda env remove -n qa-env-remove`.
   The package list is printed and there is only one prompt to confirm deletion. It defaults to `n`.
   Press Enter. The environment is still there.
3. Run that command again and answer `y`.
   The same single prompt shows, on answering `y` the environment is gone.
4. Recreate the environment and then run `conda remove -n qa-env-remove --all --keep-env`.
   Only the "Proceed?" warning to delete conda packages shows. Answer the prompt with `y`. Conda packages are deleted and the empty environment remains.
5. Now run `conda install -n qa-env-remove xz --yes`, then `conda remove -n qa-env-remove --all`.
   The package list is printed and only one deletion prompt shows. Answer with `y` and The environment is deleted.


### Pass criteria
Each step matches the result written under it.

